{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>The concubines.</b> It is written deficient — there was only one concubine: she is Hagar, she is Keturah (Bereshit Rabbah). Wives — with a marriage contract; concubines — without a marriage contract, as we say in Sanhedrin, regarding the wives and concubines of David." "<b>And Abraham gave gifts.</b> Our Sages explained: he transmitted to them a name of impurity (Sanhedrin 91). Another interpretation: what was given to him on account of Sarah, and the other gifts that were given to him — all of it he gave to them, for he did not wish to derive benefit from them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:24.324229446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}